d\", \"S_read_release\", \"S_read_queue\", \"S_log_init\", \"S_log_append\", \"S_log_apply\", \"S_log_term\", \"S_unstable\", \"S_tracker_commit\", \"S_tracker_votes\", \"S_tracker_active\", \"S_progress\", \"S_joint\", \"S_majority\", \"S_change\", \"S_change_members\", \"S_restore_config\", \"S_storage\", \"S_node\", \"S_ready_contract\", \"S_bootstrap\"], \"record\": {\"path\": \"state.json\", \"collection\": \"selections\", \"match\": {\"operation_id\": \"af1e0a73be794244af6a5dfe91d6cc0e\"}}}, {\"operation_id\": \"c89b99c432144c8ba6d4a920accb14d4\", \"action\": \"obligation\", \"candidate_ids\": [\"45d41e2405de4b028bd8a31a7e3fc9b0\"], \"answered_preview\": \"Resolved the requirement gap for a narrow implementation-semantic proposition: issuance-term obsolescence forbids entry retirement even if entry identity matches. Separated prepared completion token from external storage completion, and iso\\u2026\", \"ref_ids\": [\"S_completion_contract\", \"S_stable_contract\", \"S_ready\", \"S_election\", \"S_unstable\", \"S_config\"], \"record\": {\"path\": \"state.json\", \"collection\": \"selections\", \"match\": {\"operation_id\": \"c89b99c432144c8ba6d4a920accb14d4\"}}}, {\"operation_id\": \"9fc4b62618184d41988fa5ce0bc8dfad\", \"action\": \"check\", \"candidate_ids\": [], \"answered_preview\": \"Constructed a bounded legal schedule for the accepted Candidate and Unit. Actual producer messages are captured, old and current append jobs remain ordered, and entry identity is checked independently from issuance-term staleness. A local c\\u2026\", \"ref_ids\": [\"S_ready\", \"S_election\", \"S_bootstrap\", \"S_config\", \"S_mem_append\", \"S_mem_hardstate\", \"S_unstable\"], \"record\": {\"path\": \"state.json\", \"collection\": \"selections\", \"match\": {\"operation_id\": \"9fc4b62618184d41988fa5ce0bc8dfad\"}}}, {\"operation_id\": \"13a00938bd304ac0baa7ea8ad4bffcec\", \"action\": \"review\", \"candidate_ids\": [], \"answered_preview\": \"The trusted run reached the selected stale-completion condition and measured offset 5 before and after the old term-2 response in term 3. The actual producer, legal bootstrap/election/replication prefix, same-history term transition, ordere\\u2026\", \"ref_ids\": [\"017cd81f455948f2a0d0832a53e904e6\", \"e365efbbde80420bb1b1730a6c13d88a\", \"S_completion_contract\", \"S_election\", \"S_unstable\", \"S_membership\", \"S_responses\", \"S_read_release\"], \"record\": {\"path\": \"state.json\", \"collection\": \"selections\", \"match\": {\"operation_id\": \"13a00938bd304ac0baa7ea8ad4bffcec\"}}}, {\"operation_id\": \"682ddc634c914ff8834030c5cdca7657\", \"action\": \"explore\", \"candidate_ids\": [], \"answered_preview\": \"Read the actual pendingReadIndexMessages writers/consumer, configuration commit path and election guard. The only explicit pending-read release is after acknowledgment-driven maybeCommit; switchToConfig can commit but does not call that rel\\u2026\", \"ref_ids\": [\"S_node_advance_order\", \"S_raw_advance_contract\", \"S_pending_read_purpose\", \"S_read_api_contract\", \"S_transition\", \"S_membership\", \"S_responses\", \"S_read_release\", \"S_new_leader_read_test\"], \"record\": {\"path\": \"state.json\", \"collection\": \"selections\", \"match\": {\"operation_id\": \"682ddc634c914ff8834030c5cdca7657\"}}, \"feedback\": {\"ref_ids\": [\"S_node_advance_order\", \"S_raw_advance_contract\", \"S_pending_read_purpose\", \"S_read_api_contract\", \"S_transition\", \"S_membership\", \"S_responses\", \"S_read_release\", \"S_new_leader_read_test\"], \"answered\": \"Read the actual pendingReadIndexMessages writers/consumer, configuration commit path and election guard. The only explicit pending-read release is after acknowledgment-driven maybeCommit; switchToConfig can commit but does not call that release. A regular not-yet-advanced committed configuration prevents campaigning via hasUnappliedConfChanges. However Node.Advance explicitly permits advancing while application is in progress, while RawNode.Advance describes applied-and-saved completion and ApplyConfChange is required whenever a configuration is observed. This is a real ordering/applicability gap, not an established violation. ReadIndex also permits request loss and caller retry, so generic eventual response cannot be assumed. Built a four-node exploration with actual bootstrap, configuration proposal, early Advance, election, queued read and delayed configuration activation; local execution only guided construction.\", \"remaining\": [\"Trusted clean-copy exploration output must establish the actual prefix and observed endpoints.\", \"Resolve whether the early-Advance optimization permits deferring ApplyConfChange specifically, rather than only slower application work after membership has been updated.\", \"If that ordering is permitted, determine whether the internal queue-handling expectation supports a narrow implementation contract despite the public lossy ReadIndex contract; otherwise explain the observed conditional history as outside the valid caller order.\"], \"understanding\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Preserve the completed stale-completion result without changes. Compare (1) this concrete configuration/read interaction with known alternate campaign protection and a precise API-ordering unknown, (2) learner versus voter read quorum eligibility with explicit filtering, and (3) full delayed-storage overwrite history with longer construction. Select (1) for exploration because it can distinguish a reachable alternate commit path from an invalid caller prefix before spending an obligation. No map change or Candidate is asserted from local observations.\", \"question_updates\": {}}}]\npending_work []\ncheck {\"id\": \"4255ba1800cb475fb2eabf4eb6c26530\", \"action\": \"agent_probe\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"outcome\": \"unknown\", \"stdout\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-09-29_12-58-49-etcd_raft-real-run/logs/4255ba1800cb475fb2eabf4eb6c26530/stdout.log\", \"