{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '70,107p' ../agent-source/doc.go\nsed -n '110,125p' ../agent-source/README.md\nsed -n '290,339p' ../agent-source/rawnode_test.go\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('../state.json'))\nc=next(x for x in s['checks'] if x['id']=='cfa40e9c46064645aa6322f0a0286660')\nprint('execution',json.dumps({k:c[k] for k in ['id','status','outcome','exit_code','parameters']},indent=2))\nfor line in open(c['stdout']):\n r=json.loads(line)\n if 'CA_EVENT' in r.get('Output',''):print(r['Output'],end='')\nx=next(x for x in s['selections'] if x['operation_id']=='682ddc634c914ff8834030c5cdca7657');print('record keys',list(x));print('retained feedback remaining',x['feedback']['remaining'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '70,107p' ../agent-source/doc.go\nsed -n '110,125p' ../agent-source/README.md\nsed -n '290,339p' ../agent-source/rawnode_test.go\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('../state.json'))\nc=next(x for x in s['checks'] if x['id']=='cfa40e9c46064645aa6322f0a0286660')\nprint('execution',json.dumps({k:c[k] for k in ['id','status','outcome','exit_code','parameters']},indent=2))\nfor line in open(c['stdout']):\n r=json.loads(line)\n if 'CA_EVENT' in r.get('Output',''):print(r['Output'],end='')\nx=next(x for x in s['selections'] if x['operation_id']=='682ddc634c914ff8834030c5cdca7657');print('record keys',list(x));print('retained feedback remaining',x['feedback']['remaining'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"\nFirst, you must read from the Node.Ready() channel and process the updates\nit contains. These steps may be performed in parallel, except as noted in step\n2.\n\n1. Write HardState, Entries, and Snapshot to persistent storage if they are\nnot empty. Note that when writing an Entry with Index i, any\npreviously-persisted entries with Index >= i must be discarded.\n\n2. Send all Messages to the nodes named in the To field. It is important that\nno messages be sent until the latest HardState has been persisted to disk,\nand all Entries written by any previous Ready batch (Messages may be sent while\nentries from the same batch are being persisted). To reduce the I/O latency, an\noptimization can be applied to make leader write to disk in parallel with its\nfollowers (as explained at section 10.2.1 in Raft thesis). If any Message has type\nMsgSnap, call Node.ReportSnapshot() after it has been sent (these messages may be\nlarge).\n\nNote: Marshalling messages is not thread-safe; it is important that you\nmake sure that no new entries are persisted while marshalling.\nThe easiest way to achieve this is to serialize the messages directly inside\nyour main raft loop.\n\n3. Apply Snapshot (if any) and CommittedEntries to the state machine.\nIf any committed Entry has Type EntryConfChange, call Node.ApplyConfChange()\nto apply it to the node. The configuration change may be cancelled at this point\nby setting the NodeID field to zero before calling ApplyConfChange\n(but ApplyConfChange must be called one way or the other, and the decision to cancel\nmust be based solely on the state machine and not external information such as\nthe observed health of the node).\n\n4. Call Node.Advance() to signal readiness for the next batch of updates.\nThis may be done at any time after step 1, although all updates must be processed\nin the order they were returned by Ready.\n\nSecond, all persisted log entries must be made available via an\nimplementation of the Storage interface. The provided MemoryStorage\ntype can be used for this (if you repopulate its state upon a\n```\n\nAfter creating a Node, the user has a few responsibilities:\n\nFirst, read from the Node.Ready() channel and process the updates it contains. These steps may be performed in parallel, except as noted in step 2.\n\n1. Write Entries, HardState and Snapshot to persistent storage in order, i.e. Entries first, then HardState and Snapshot if they are not empty. If persistent storage supports atomic writes then all of them can be written together. Note that when writing an Entry with Index i, any previously-persisted entries with Index >= i must be discarded.\n\n2. Send all Messages to the nodes named in the To field. It is important that no messages be sent until the latest HardState has been persisted to disk, and all Entries written by any previous Ready batch (Messages may be sent while entries from the same batch are being persisted). To reduce the I/O latency, an optimization can be applied to make leader write to disk in parallel with its followers (as explained at section 10.2.1 in Raft thesis). If any Message has type MsgSnap, call Node.ReportSnapshot() after it has been sent (these messages may be large). Note: Marshalling messages is not thread-safe; it is important to make sure that no new entries are persisted while marshalling. The easiest way to achieve this is to serialise the messages directly inside the main raft loop.\n\n3. Apply Snapshot (if any) and CommittedEntries to the state machine. If any committed Entry has Type EntryConfChange, call Node.ApplyConfChange() to apply it to the node. The configuration change may be cancelled at this point by setting the NodeID field to zero before calling ApplyConfChange (but ApplyConfChange must be called one way or the other, and the decision to cancel must be based solely on the state machine and not external information such as the observed health of the node).\n\n4. Call Node.Advance() to signal readiness for the next batch of updates. This may be done at any time after step 1, although all updates must be processed in the order they were returned by Ready.\n\nSecond, all persisted log entries must be made available via an implementation of the Storage interface. The provided MemoryStorage type can be used for this (if repopulating its state upon a restart), or a custom disk-backed implementation can be supplied.\n\n\t\t\tassert.Equal(t, ccdata, entries[1].Data)\n\n\t\t\trequire.Equal(t, &tc.exp, cs)\n\n\t\t\tvar maybePlusOne uint64\n\t\t\tif autoLeave, ok := tc.cc.AsV2().EnterJoint(); ok && autoLeave {\n\t\t\t\t// If this is an auto-leaving joint conf change, it will have\n\t\t\t\t// appended the entry that auto-leaves, so add one to the last\n\t\t\t\t// index that forms the basis of our expectations on\n\t\t\t\t// pendingConfIndex. (Recall that lastIndex was taken from stable\n\t\t\t\t// storage, but this auto-leaving entry isn't on stable storage\n\t\t\t\t// yet).\n\t\t\t\tmaybePlusOne = 1\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\trequire.Equal(t, lastIndex+maybePlusOne, rawNode.raft.pendingConfIndex)\n\n\t\t\t// Move the RawNode along. If the ConfChange was simple, nothing else\n\t\t\t// should happen. Otherwise, we're in a joint state, which is either\n\t\t\t// left automatically or not. If not, we add the proposal that leaves\n\t\t\t// it manually.\n\t\t\trd := rawNode.Ready()\n\t\t\tvar context []byte\n\t\t\tif !tc.exp.AutoLeave {\n\t\t\t\trequire.Empty(t, rd.Entries)\n\t\t\t\trawNode.Advance(rd)\n\t\t\t\tif tc.exp2 == nil {\n\t\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tcontext = []byte(\"manual\")\n\t\t\t\tt.Log(\"leaving joint state manually\")\n\t\t\t\trequire.NoError(t, rawNode.ProposeConfChange(pb.ConfChangeV2{Context: context}))\n\t\t\t\trd = rawNode.Ready()\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t// Check that the right ConfChange comes out.\n\t\t\trequire.Len(t, rd.Entries, 1)\n\t\t\trequire.Equal(t, pb.EntryConfChangeV2, rd.Entries[0].Type)\n\t\t\tvar cc pb.ConfChangeV2\n\t\t\trequire.NoError(t, cc.Unmarshal(rd.Entries[0].Data))\n\t\t\trequire.Equal(t, pb.ConfChangeV2{Context: context}, cc)\n\n\t\t\t// Lie and pretend the ConfChange applied. It won't do so because now\n\t\t\t// we require the joint quorum and we're only running one node.\n\t\t\tcs = rawNode.ApplyConfChange(cc)\n\t\t\trequire.Equal(t, tc.exp2, cs)\n\n\t\t\trawNode.Advance(rd)\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\nexecution {\n  \"id\": \"cfa40e9c46064645aa6322f0a0286660\",\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"outcome\": \"tests_passed\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"parameters\": {\n    \"timeout_limit\": \"action_timeout\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 600.0,\n    \"execution_backend\": {\n      \"name\": \"go_module\",\n      \"version\": \"2\",\n      \"support_files\": []\n    }\n  }\n}\nCA_EVENT {\"applied\":6,\"committed\":6,\"delayed_config_index\":6,\"event\":\"config_read_exploration\",\"node\":2,\"stage\":\"early_advance\",\"voters\":[1,2,3,4]}\nCA_EVENT {\"committed\":6,\"event\":\"config_read_exploration\",\"last_index\":7,\"match_peer3\":7,\"match_self\":7,\"node\":2,\"old_read_results\":0,\"pending_reads\":1,\"stage\":\"before_activation\",\"term\":3}\nCA_EVENT {\"committed\":7,\"event\":\"config_read_exploration\",\"node\":2,\"old_read_results\":0,\"pending_reads\":1,\"stage\":\"after_activation\",\"term\":3,\"voters\":[1,2,3]}\nCA_EVENT {\"committed\":7,\"event\":\"config_read_exploration\",\"fresh_read_results\":1,\"network_pending\":0,\"node\":2,\"old_read_results\":0,\"pending_reads\":1,\"stage\":\"after_heartbeats_and_fresh_read\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"committed\":8,\"event\":\"config_read_exploration\",\"fresh_read_results\":1,\"network_pending\":0,\"node\":2,\"old_read_results\":1,\"pending_reads\":0,\"stage\":\"after_later_proposal\"}\nrecord keys ['operation_id', 'action', 'rationale', 'feedback', 'map_updated', 'map_changes', 'accepted_versions', 'candidate_ids']\nretained feedback remaining ['Trusted clean-copy exploration output must establish the actual prefix and observed endpoints.', 'Resolve whether the early-Advance optimization permits deferring ApplyConfChange specifically, rather than only slower application work after membership has been updated.', 'If that ordering is permitted, determine whether the internal queue-handling expectation supports a narrow implementation contract despite the public lossy ReadIndex contract; otherwise explain the observed conditional history as outside the valid caller order.']\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The clean-copy exploration reached the sequence: configuration activation advanced commit from 6 to 7, but the older read stayed in the pre-commit queue. A fresh read completed; the older read completed after a later proposal committed.\n\nThe package guide explicitly allows `Advance` after persistence, with application kept in order. I’ll use that as the basis for a narrow queue-transition obligation, while retaining the differing RawNode wording and the public API’s permission to lose read requests.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > make_read_obligation.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v2.json'))\nfor a in m['activities']:a.pop('behavior_ids',None)\nfor f in m['facts']:\n for k in ['established_by','consumed_by']:f.pop(k,None)\nnewsrc=[dict(id='S_early_advance_usage',file='doc.go',start_line=70,end_line=103,kind='document_statement'),dict(id='S_early_advance_readme',file='README.md',start_line=112,end_line=122,kind='document_statement')]\nm['behaviors'] += [dict(id='B_read_wait',primary_activity='A1',execution_owner='RawNode.ReadIndex -> raft.stepLeader',protocol_context='Leader term, nonsingleton voter configuration and no committed entry from current term',trigger='MsgReadIndex while committedEntryInCurrentTerm is false',implementation_guards=['Singleton fast path precedes the current-term check.','For nonsingleton leaders, current committed entry log term must equal leader term before entering the normal read protocol.'],writes=['Append actual read message to pendingReadIndexMessages.'],produces_fact_ids=['F_read_wait'],important_branches=['Already-qualified request directly calls sendMsgReadIndexResponse.','Follower forwards to known leader or drops when none; public ReadIndex permits request loss and retry.'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'Read authority confirmation is deferred until the newly elected leader has established its current-term committed prefix.','A7':'Queued admission does not produce a ReadState or promise unconditional eventual client completion.'},source_ids=['S_proposal','S_read_raw_entry','S_read_api_contract','S_read','S_pending_read_purpose']),dict(id='B_read_release',primary_activity='A1',execution_owner='stepLeader MsgAppResp branch -> releasePendingReadIndexMessages -> sendMsgReadIndexResponse',protocol_context='Leader with newly advanced commit and current-term committed entry',trigger='Acknowledgment-driven maybeCommit returns true',implementation_guards=['No pending messages is a no-op; function rejects release unless committedEntryInCurrentTerm.'],reads=['pendingReadIndexMessages, committed index/log term and read option.'],writes=['Clear pre-commit queue and submit each saved request to normal read processing.'],consumes_fact_ids=['F_read_wait'],external_effects=['Safe mode records request context and committed index, self-acknowledges, and broadcasts heartbeat with context; lease mode can respond directly.'],important_branches=['The switchToConfig maybeCommit caller broadcasts appends but has no call to this release function.','Tick/heartbeat and new already-qualified reads use the separate readOnly queue, not pendingReadIndexMessages.'],cross_activity_effects={'A7':'Makes previously gated requests available to the ordinary read-result production path without a new client invocation.'},source_ids=['S_responses','S_read_release','S_membership','S_replicate','S_read_queue','S_read']),dict(id='B_safe_read_result',primary_activity='A1',execution_owner='stepLeader MsgHeartbeatResp -> readOnly.recvAck/advance -> responseToReadIndexReq',protocol_context='ReadOnlySafe request context, active voter quorum and current message term',trigger='Heartbeat acknowledgment with nonempty context matching a registered read request',implementation_guards=['Sender must have progress; Step processes terms before leader handler.','Voters.VoteResult must win; learner progress alone is not a vote in the voter configuration.'],writes=['Record acknowledgment, advance the context queue and create ReadState or MsgReadIndexResp.'],important_branches=['Acknowledgment map is distinct from pre-commit message queue; a fresh read cannot advance requests that were never entered into the map.','Context-keyed requests can piggyback earlier queue entries.'],cross_activity_effects={'A7':'Produces request-correlated index used by caller after sufficient local application.'},source_ids=['S_responses','S_read_queue','S_read','S_joint','S_majority','S_ready_contract'])]\nm['facts'].append(dict(id='F_read_wait',meaning='A specific read request message has been retained in pendingReadIndexMessages because the leader has not yet committed a log entry in its current term. Retention is not read quorum support or a completed ReadState.',identity={'owner':'Raft instance holding the queue','request':'Message From and Entries[0].Data request context; the selected check uses a fresh unique context','queue':'pendingReadIndexMessages, distinct from readOnly.pendingReadIndex'},validity_context='Retained across reset because reset replaces readOnly but does not clear this queue. Release rechecks the current leader term against the committed entry term.',representation=['r.pendingReadIndexMessages'],invalidators=[],reinterpreters=['B_authority'],durability='Volatile request retention; not restored from storage.',recovery='Public API permits loss and client retries. No durable request reconstruction.',source_ids=['S_pending_read_purpose','S_proposal','S_read_release','S_transition','S_read_api_contract'],unknowns=['Whether every commit-producing path discharges the current-term gate is the selected question.','This Fact is not a guarantee of eventual public response.']))\nm['surfaces'].append(dict(entry_point='Early Advance -> delayed ApplyConfChange -> switchToConfig first current-term commit',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B_read_wait','B_read_release','B_safe_read_result','B_membership','B_apply','B_authority'],reason='The tracked applied index used by campaign guard can advance before physical application under the documented synchronous early-Advance optimization. Configuration activation can then supply an alternate first-commit path; its pending-read interaction needs a scoped check.',source_ids=['S_early_advance_usage','S_node_advance_order','S_raw_advance_contract','S_transition','S_membership','S_read_release'],high_consequence=True))\nm['core_overview']['connection']['explanation'] += ' In synchronous Ready/Advance usage, the documented early-Advance optimization can acknowledge application progress before slow application work finishes; therefore the campaign guard is a check of the tracked applied index, not independent observation of actual ApplyConfChange completion. Under that caller ordering, delayed membership activation is a separate potential first-current-term commit path; pre-commit read messages and the normal quorum-confirmation queue remain distinct.'\nm['core_overview']['connection']['source_ids'] += ['S_early_advance_usage','S_node_advance_order','S_raw_advance_contract','S_pending_read_purpose']\nm['core_overview']['connection']['behavior_ids'] += ['B_read_wait','B_read_release','B_safe_read_result']\nm['core_overview']['connection']['fact_ids'] += ['F_read_wait']\nm['core_overview']['open_details'].append('Early Advance is explicitly permitted by package/Node usage documentation, while RawNode.Advance tersely describes applied-and-saved completion. The selected synchronous interpretation and the public ReadIndex loss allowance must remain explicit in applicability review.')\njson.dump(m,open('read-wait-map.json','w'),indent=2)\nq=dict(question='For a retained ReadOnlySafe request waiting for first current-term commitment, does configuration activation that establishes that commitment discharge the pre-commit gate, or does the request remain dependent on another proposal despite normal read quorum work being available?',importance='A request retained behind an already-satisfied leader-read prerequisite can wait for unrelated write traffic while fresh reads succeed. This concerns local read-processing semantics and potential latency in read-mostly deployments; it is not a stale-read or general liveness finding.',source_ids=[],participants=['Leader RawNode','Caller applying an already committed configuration','Voters supplying actual replication and heartbeat responses'],objects=['pendingReadIndexMessages entry','Current-term committed prefix','Applied voter configuration','Ready.ReadStates request contexts'],contexts=['ReadOnlySafe and nonsingleton configuration','Synchronous Ready/Advance with documented early-Advance optimization','Ordered actual application and no crash'],event_paths=['Committed membership change -> persistence and early Advance -> actual election with old active configuration -> first-current-term entry below old quorum -> ReadIndex retained -> delayed ApplyConfChange changes quorum and commits current-term entry','Process emitted append/heartbeat work -> fresh read completes independently -> later proposal advances commit and releases retained request'],activity_classes=['A1','A4','A5','A7'],behavior_ids=['B_read_wait','B_read_release'],fact_ids=['F_read_wait'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B_membership':'Activation reinterprets retained progress under the new quorum and can satisfy the current-term commit prerequisite.','B_authority':'Election is guarded by tracked applied index, and produces the new leader/term.','B_apply':'Advance updates tracked application while documented caller optimization may leave configuration application in progress.','B_propose':'Real proposals create the membership change and later release control.','B_commit':'Current-term quorum aggregation supplies the first-commit predicate.','B_safe_read_result':'Produces request-correlated Ready results after normal read quorum processing; fresh read acts as endpoint control.','B_recover':'Real bootstrap supplies initial membership without assigned protocol state.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['hasUnappliedConfChanges blocks campaigning when a committed configuration is still tracked as unapplied.','The normal MsgAppResp maybeCommit path explicitly releases pending reads.','ReadIndex publicly permits request loss and caller retry; no unconditional eventual response is owed.','RawNode.Advance says applied-and-saved, whereas Node/package documentation explicitly permits early Advance.'],unknowns=['Formal monitored execution and correspondence review of the narrow queue-transition requirement remain outstanding.','Applicability interprets the explicit package/Node early-Advance permission as covering delayed configuration application while preserving application order; stricter configuration-specific ordering would exclude the constructed prefix.','No client latency bound, stale read, crash behavior or general liveness consequence is established.'],priority=2,trigger_rationale='The accepted frontier selected the asymmetry between acknowledgment-driven and configuration-driven commit. Exploration cfa40e9c46064645aa6322f0a0286660 executed the latter under early Advance and observed retained pre-commit state until another proposal. The requirement is separately based on S_pending_read_purpose; exploratory output motivates the question but is not property Evidence.',disposition='ready_for_check',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\nids=set(['S_early_advance_usage','S_early_advance_readme','S_node_advance_order','S_raw_advance_contract','S_new_leader_read_test'])\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id'] in q['behavior_ids'] or b['id'] in q['supporting_behavior_ids']:ids.update(b['source_ids'])\nids.update(m['facts'][-1]['source_ids']);q['source_ids']=sorted(ids)\nclaim=dict(id='C_read_gate_release',kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='A ReadOnlySafe request retained solely because its leader has not committed an entry in its current term must leave that pre-commit gate for normal read processing when the first current-term commitment is established. Configuration-driven commitment must not leave such a retained request gated on an additional log commitment.',source_ids=['S_pending_read_purpose','S_new_leader_read_test','S_read_api_contract','S_read_release','S_membership','S_early_advance_usage','S_node_advance_order','S_raw_advance_contract'],scope=dict(description='Pre-commit queue transition for a retained request on a nonsingleton leader, including commitment triggered by applying an already committed configuration. Synchronous Ready/Advance caller using the documented early-Advance optimization; actual application remains ordered.',assumptions=['Serialized RawNode methods, authentic peer messages and a stable leader during the measured transition.','Ready entries/HardState are persisted before Advance and messages; actual committed-entry application remains in log order.','The explicit package/Node permission to Advance after persistence while application is in progress applies through RawNode\\\\'s documented correspondence to Node.','Unique request contexts, ReadOnlySafe, no process or storage crash.'],excluded=['Unconditional public ReadIndex completion; requests can be lost per API.','A time bound or general liveness result.','Linearizability violation, lease-based reads, concurrent context reuse and joint-configuration exhaustive coverage.']),pending=['Execute a fixed direct checker for pre-commit queue membership after the actual first-current-term transition.'],grounding=dict(source_ids=['S_proposal','S_read_release','S_membership','S_transition','S_ready','S_api'],expectation_ids=['S_pending_read_purpose','S_new_leader_read_test','S_early_advance_usage','S_node_advance_order','S_read_api_contract','S_raw_advance_contract'],derivation='S_pending_read_purpose states that these retained messages will be handled as soon as the first log entry is committed in the current term. S_new_leader_read_test expects the postponed request to be processed once that prerequisite is satisfied. The obligation is the internal prerequisite transition, not a stronger promise that all ReadIndex invocations complete. S_early_advance_usage says Advance may occur at any time after persistence and associates ApplyConfChange with application step 3; S_node_advance_order expressly allows in-progress application but prohibits out-of-order application. S_api states RawNode methods correspond to Node and are described more fully there. This gives an explicit source basis for the selected early-Advance interpretation, independent of the observed missing release.',applicability='The request is demonstrably retained in the pre-commit queue, rather than lost or not admitted. A legal quorum changes through application of a real committed configuration, and actual Ready work and heartbeat responses are delivered. No direct protocol-state assignments or timer-based deadline are needed.',conflicts=['S_raw_advance_contract describes Advance as applied-and-saved, whereas S_early_advance_usage and S_node_advance_order permit Advance before application finishes. The scope adopts the explicit optimization permission and keeps this documentation tension visible.'],alternatives=['Applying configuration before Advance keeps the campaign guard effective and avoids this particular prefix.','Public retry may produce a new successful read without discharging the originally retained queue entry; that does not prove the queue-transition contract.','An additional current-term proposal can later trigger the ordinary release path.'],unresolved=['A stricter interpretation requiring configuration activation before early Advance would exclude this prefix; correspondence review must adjudicate that interpretation from the captured API documentation.']))\nbindings=[]\nfor id,mat,symbol,lo,hi,desc in [('BIND_read_wait','S_proposal','stepLeader',1346,1365,'Produces the retained request when current-term commitment is absent.'),('BIND_config_commit','S_membership','switchToConfig',1975,2031,'Activates configuration and calls maybeCommit, without invoking pre-commit read release.'),('BIND_read_release','S_read_release','releasePendingReadIndexMessages',2123,2140,'Defines gate discharge and transfer into normal read processing.'),('BIND_read_ack_release','S_responses','stepLeader',1542,1547,'Normal acknowledgment-driven commit invokes the release, supplying a positive control.')]:\n bindings.append(dict(i